/-!
# The small Sylow bound in the exceptional amalgam branch

The coset argument and its exceptional-vertex application prove that the
common Sylow subgroup has order at most sixteen whenever either vertex
fails characteristic two. This includes the mixed branch and its literal
G/O₂(G) application. The exceptional amalgam identifications remain separate.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, F.6.5, printed pp.304--305.
-/
